  "claim_short": "2002.03974 Ambrus Bai Hou Uniform tight frames as optimal signals Problem 1 candidate full arbitrary-noise solution. Put alpha=(N-d)/d and c_sigma=clip(sigma/sqrt(alpha),c1,c2). Exact optimal capacity log(1+1/(sigma^2/c_sigma+alpha*c_sigma)); all maximizers for N>d are uniform tight frames of common squared norm c_sigma. Proof weights reciprocal SINR D_i by x_i=1/|v_i|^2, uses a_j/a_i+a_i/a_j>=2, the Welch...",
